orks, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "bf36b7250111bb22e77eaff3f6472f74bf2345969b5192e8ac0914745a6ca9b3", "hash": "633d99582d906ad68250b3a6c5e7628d0af7be63f38b0bce8fe699c4e02b05b5"}, {"seq": 2890, "time": "2026-10-29T00:47:11.558934+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 32012, "provider_input_hash": "c9c7d20bfc1bde7a943d324a3f1b0710455b632c47684976e6befbc95c20e023", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-c6ded2